                <invention-title lang="de">VERFAHREN UND VORRICHTUNG ZUR UPLINK (UL)-MULTIPLEXIERUNG UND PRIORISIERUNG IN EINER NEW RADIO (NR)-KOMMUNIKATION</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">PROCÉDÉS ET APPAREIL DE MULTIPLEXAGE ET DE PRIORISATION DE LIAISON MONTANTE (UL) DANS UNE COMMUNICATION NOUVELLE RADIO (NR)</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">METHODS AND APPARATUS FOR UPLINK (UL) MULTIPLEXING AND PRIORITIZATION IN NEW RADIO (NR) COMMUNICATION</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A wireless transmit/receive unit (WTRU) may receive, via radio resource control (RRC) signaling, an indication of a set of reference frequency resources for which uplink cancellation could occur, an indication of at least one priority for which uplink cancellation is applicable, and an allocation for a configured grant, the allocation for the configured grant comprising a frequency allocation for the configured grant, a time allocation for the configured grant, and a priority index for the configured grant. Also, the WTRU may receive a physical downlink control channel (PDCCH) transmission, the PDCCH comprising downlink control information (DCI), the DCI comprising cancellation indication (CI) information, wherein the Cl information indicates that a subset of the set of reference frequency resources is subject to uplink cancellation in one or more time symbols. Also, the WTRU may cancel at least part of an uplink transmission associated with the configured grant based on the Cl information, the frequency allocation for the configured grant, the time allocation for the configured grant, the priority index for the configured grant, and the indication of the at least one priority for which uplink cancellation is applicable received in the RRC signaling</p>
            </abstract>
